This notes is for the RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) implementation in the JobSearchAI project.
The purpose is optimize the retrieval process to use function calling to optimize the user search prompts instead of using
regex and text process.

1. **Optimizing The Function that sends job data to the LLM**:
        a. The function generate_recommendations() used to accept a dictionary.
            i. I am going to make it accept a list of dictionaries instead. This will allow the LLM to process multiple job data at once,
               which is more efficient and can provide better recommendations.
        b. The function calls the parse_response() function to parse the LLM's response, and returns a list of dictionaries.
            i. I have modified it to return a python list of dictionaries instead, by using json.loads() to convert the JSON string into a Python list of dictionaries.
            Remember to change your system prompt to instruct the LLM to return a list of dictionaries instead of a single dictionary.
            ii. While checking, remember to also test if it is relevant to provide the output schema in the api call or just
            leave it as `text = {"format": {"type": "json_object"}}`

